From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] smbios: avoid the legacy PC memory scan on non-x86 systems

The fixed 0xf0000 BIOS area is not a portable firmware discovery interface.
On an AArch64 DT-only tablet, pread fails and the following mmap succeeds but
faults with SIGBUS when copied. Keep normal firmware-table detection and the
legacy x86 fallback; return unavailable on other architectures.

--- a/src/common/impl/smbios.c
+++ b/src/common/impl/smbios.c
@@ -270,6 +270,12 @@
 } FFSmbiosEntryPoint;
 
 static bool fillTableBufferFallback(FFstrbuf* buffer) {
+    #if !defined(__i386__) && !defined(__x86_64__)
+    // The legacy PC BIOS memory window is not defined on this architecture.
+    // Normal firmware-table discovery runs before this fallback.
+    FF_DEBUG("Legacy PC SMBIOS memory scan is unavailable on this architecture");
+    return false;
+    #endif
     const char* devMem =
     #if __HAIKU__
         "/dev/misc/mem";
